SIM-23: keep full-precision heads for the output file's head loss

EN_solveQ writes the binary output file from the scratch hydraulics
file, which stores heads as 4-byte floats. Head loss and friction factor
are differences of those heads, so in lightly loaded pipes they lose most
of their digits or become 0. Keep a copy of the heads as doubles in a
second scratch file while the hydraulics run, and let readhyd() use it.
The hydraulics file itself is unchanged, so EN_savehydfile, EN_usehydfile
and EPANET-MSX, which reads that file directly, are not affected. With a
file from EN_usehydfile there is no copy, and the heads stay 4-byte.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply SIM-23_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
